Short:        Counts the calls programs make to libs
Uploader:     (We fill this in at upload time)
Author:       Dalsin Limited
Type:         dev/debug
Version:      1.0
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 2.0.4
Distribution: Aminet

LibCount counts how often each function of the libraries you name is called,
while you use the machine, then prints one line per function: library, offset
and count.

  LibCount graphics.library intuition.library layers.library SECONDS 30 TO
  RAM:counts

Each function gets a 12-byte stub that adds one and jumps on to the original,
put in with SetFunction() under Forbid() with the caches cleared. At the end a
stub comes out only if nothing patched that function after it; otherwise it
stays and keeps passing calls through. Ctrl-C ends the count early.

libcount_report.py (Python 3, on a PC) names the offsets from the NDK's FD
files and sorts them into a table.

It was written to find which graphics, intuition and layers calls Workbench
and programs really make on an RTG screen, for OpenRTG.

